    <item>
      <link>https://www.forbes.com/sites/insights-acxiom/2026/10/21/3-ways-to-move-enterprise-ai-from-ambition-to-action/</link>
      <title>3 Ways To Move Enterprise AI From Ambition To Action</title>
      <description>A Forbes Insights survey of business leaders shows many companies face uncertainties regarding human roles, fragmented data, and legacy practices when deploying agentic AI. Successful deployment requires a strategic human orchestrator, employee buy-in, and a strong data foundation. Currently, only 18% of companies report that data effectively influences AI-driven marketing decision-making.</description>
      <dc:creator>Acxiom Contributor, Insights Contributor</dc:creator>
      <atom:author>
        <atom:name>Acxiom Contributor, Insights Contributor</atom:name>
        <atom:uri>https://www.forbes.com/sites/insights-acxiom/people/acxiomcontributor/</atom:uri>
      </atom:author>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">content_6ad8c8b973c36387d5b2711e</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:19:47 -0400</pubDate>
      <atom:updated>2026-10-21T10:29:26-04:00</atom:updated>
      <content:encoded>A Forbes Insights survey of business leaders shows many companies face uncertainties regarding human roles, fragmented data, and legacy practices when deploying agentic AI. Successful deployment requires a strategic human orchestrator, employee buy-in, and a strong data foundation. Currently, only 18% of companies report that data effectively influences AI-driven marketing decision-making.</content:encoded>
      <media:content url="https://imageio.forbes.com/specials-images/imageserve/6ad8c90135bc4e684bbfbf37/0x0.jpg" medium="image">
